{"id":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"Deferrals","desc":"NO DEFERRALS (the human, 2026-08-22): a PR ships everything its item names and everything it spots in touched code; what cannot be done STOPS and ASKS. The Inbox holds only what the human chooses to park. ONE exception, ruled 2026-08-22 11:57: tests found flaky on master that a PR does not own go under the child node `flaky tests`, one entry per file, each dispatched as its own lane.","created":"2026-08-21T17:25:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T16:13:09-04:00"}
{"id":"chatentry-kind-union","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"ChatEntry becomes a union discriminated on kind #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T19:43:21-04:00","desc":"- ChatEntry is a flat struct with a dozen kind-specific optional fields, while its own docstring claims 'a union of six kinds' — so consumers (running.ts, statusOf) must re-establish facts the type should carry (status means nothing on a non-call row; a server-defaulted field re-defaulted client-side).\n- Discriminating the wire type on kind touches the transcript writer, every consumer's narrowing, and the wire contract — a design the human must rule, not a fold-in (#324's author argued it; grok's review concurred: a standing shape, not a cleanup that work parked).","created":"2026-08-21T17:18:39-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T19:43:21-04:00","custom":{"from":"#324","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~17:3x (question tool) — TYPE-ONLY: the union is compile-time over the unchanged encoding (wire and stored bytes identical, no migration); and the consumers' now-redundant defensive re-checks are DELETED in the same PR"}}
{"id":"filter-ask-carries-revision","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a1","title":"A filtered page re-searches the whole vault every frame #needs-brainstorm #deferral","done":"2026-08-21T17:45:44-04:00","desc":"- Measured in #290 on a 90k-node vault: one bulk gesture costs nine whole-vault search calls, one per frame. No client-side coalescing window can honestly reduce it (built both ways, measured 9→8, deleted).\n- The fix is on the server side: either the ask carries the page's revision so an unmoved set is answered from what was already computed, or the narrowing moves to the server with the reading.\n- Wants a short design note first: which of the two, the wire shape, and what the reconnect re-ask becomes.","see":["reactivity-kolu-upstream"],"created":"2026-08-20T14:01:11-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T17:45:44-04:00","custom":{"from":"olai #290 deferral","pr":"#325 merged a1302bbf — the narrowing rides the page's revision pulse; 9 whole-vault asks → 0, wire 31534→1873 kB on the 90k gesture; design note docs/brainstorming/filter-rides-the-page.md; the residual shownOf question filed as shownof-twice from=#325"}}
{"id":"shownof-twice","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a2","title":"shownOf runs twice per revision on a filtered page #deferral #human","done":"2026-08-21T17:52:31-04:00","desc":"- After #325, the narrowing rides the page's revision pulse — but computing it walks shownOf a second time per revision on a filtered page.\n- Both cures are costed in #325's design note §7: collapse to ONE member (~52 kB per keystroke against ~3 kB — declined by the author's own numbers) or a (revision, request)-keyed cache (new state no other reading has, in front of a walk that is now O(page)).\n- Wants the human's ruling: accept the double walk (it is now the right size), or buy one of the cures.","created":"2026-08-21T17:29:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T17:52:31-04:00","custom":{"from":"#325","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~17:5x (question tool) — ACCEPTED: the double walk is O(page) after #325 and cheap; both cures measured and neither free (one-member ~52 kB/keystroke; the cache is new state no other reading has). Closed without work; revisit only if a profile ever shows it."}}
{"id":"chat-refused-open-state","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a3","title":"The chat panel's state when a conversation could not be opened #deferral #human","done":"2026-08-21T19:37:59-04:00","desc":"- #331 fixed 'errored prompt reported as gone' for the prompt path; changeSession and boot in chat.ts still report ANY failure as status: gone — a refused session/new or session/load says 'not running' about a live agent.\n- The honest state after a refused load is not idle either: agent.ts's load-calls entered before the request, so a refusal leaves the module pointing at a conversation the agent rejected. Saying ready over that is worse than saying not running.\n- The fix needs a design ruling first: what IS the panel in when a conversation could not be opened — a distinct refused state with its own face? fall back to the previous conversation? something else?","created":"2026-08-21T19:03:19-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T19:37:59-04:00","custom":{"from":"#331","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~19:06 (question tool) — a DISTINCT REFUSED FACE: the panel gets an honest third state (couldn't open this conversation + the reason + retry), the agent still shown running, the module no longer pointing at the rejected conversation. Disposition: FOLD into #331's address round (same author, PR still open pre-review)."}}
{"id":"kolu-upgrade-headers","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a4","title":"Upstream: serveSurfaceApp exposes selected upgrade-request headers to the connection #deferral #kolu-upstream #human","done":"2026-08-22T04:43:30-04:00","desc":"- The live wire is a websocket; kolu's serveSurfaceApp owns the upgrade and hands no request headers to the per-connection services context — so connection-scoped identity (the trusted header at upgrade time) cannot be read there.\n- #330 works around it honestly: the chip and any plain-HTTP door (the /who endpoint, /capture) read headers directly; only a tab that should not have to GET /olai/who needs the upstream change.\n- Kolu-repo work — needs the human's ratification before any dispatch. Small: expose a selected-header allowlist on the connection context.","created":"2026-08-21T19:15:49-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T04:43:30-04:00","custom":{"from":"#330","pr":"kolu#2196 merged 58c68bdf — serveSurfaceApp takes `upgradeHeaders` (an allowlist named at serve time); SurfaceAppConnection carries { id, url, remoteAddress, headers } generic in the allowlist's names instead of the raw IncomingMessage; bad/duplicate/set-cookie names refused at boot; green on both platforms; one deferral filed (forwarded-for-fold-spelling); the olai consumer change filed as upgrade-headers-consumer","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~21:57 — QUEUED into the overnight campaign (lane-kuh, queue-4): kolu-repo PR by Opus, auto-merge on green + reviews per the campaign's policy"}}
{"id":"bundle-reserved-prefix","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a5","title":"The bundle can collide with a vault: /index.html and /assets/ at the root are unreachable pages — move the bundle under a reserved prefix #deferral","done":"2026-08-22T03:51:57-04:00","desc":"- Since addresses became prefix-free (#256), the server hands the SPA shell to anything it does not serve itself; the bundle's own paths sit at the root (`@kolu/surface-app`). **Corrected 2026-08-22 by #341's measurement:** a vault's top-level `index.html` is NOT shadowed — `GET /index.html` answers the same `no-store` shell `/` does and the client then opens the vault file as a page. What IS shadowed is `/assets/*`: a vault file under `assets/` entered as an address 404s from the immutable-asset route (client-side navigation to it works, because that is a route). The original claim named both; only the second was true.\n- Fix: move the bundle's own paths under a reserved prefix — `/_olai/assets/` (olai's own namespace, where it already mints its files). The serve half of `@kolu/surface-app` already took `assetPrefix`; the Bun BUILD had no producer for it — so the socket is upstream: kolu#2197 (the build takes the same prefix the server takes, default `/assets/`). olai #341 carries the determination, the corrected routes.ts paragraph, and the `assets/` 404 asserted as it stands (to be flipped by the follow-up). The olai consumer bump (pass the prefix to build + serve, flip the test) is a FOLLOW-UP once kolu#2197 merges and npins moves.\n- Out of this node's scope, for the human: olai's own routes shadow the same way — `/media/` is a prefix like `/assets/` (a vault folder named `media/` has no page); `/capture`, `/mcp` exact paths; `/olai/who` 204; `/olai/resync` is POST-only and not shadowed. A new node if the whole reserved-word question is wanted.","created":"2026-08-21T21:43:09-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T03:51:57-04:00","custom":{"from":"#256","pr":"olai #341 merged 0f1aab2c (the determination + corrected claim + asserted assets/ 404) and kolu#2197 merged 855df636 (the Bun build takes the asset prefix its server already takes); the olai consumer bump is filed as bundle-prefix-consumer","ruled":"the human 2026-08-21 ~21:57 — QUEUED into the overnight campaign (lane-brp, queue-5): olai first; upstream PR in kolu only if the serve contract must move"}}
{"id":"forwarded-for-fold-spelling","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a6","title":"kolu: pickUpgradeHeaders folds a repeated header with ', ' while @kolu/surface's forwardedForOf uses ',' — unify the fold (touches a @kolu/surface public export; needs the paired drishti PR) #deferral #kolu-upstream #human","done":"2026-08-22T09:59:19-04:00","desc":"Named in kolu#2196's ## Deferrals (the surface-app upgradeHeaders allowlist, overnight 2026-08-22). Two spellings of the same fold for a repeated header; the seam cannot reach the divergence today. Ruling wanted: fold it in kolu#2196 with the paired drishti PR, file it as its own kolu item, or let it lie with the comment.","created":"2026-08-22T02:58:36-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T09:59:19-04:00","custom":{"author-offer":"the author will open the drishti pair and fold it in on the human's word","from":"kolu#2196","pr":"kolu#2198 merged 66d38bb2 — the array-join dropped, an array-shaped upgrade header refused, one fold spelling left; merged on the human's word without waiting for the second CI run","why-godly":"both fixes change a @kolu/surface public export and trip the paired-drishti-PR gate; the divergent branch is unreachable today (node folds repeated x-forwarded-for itself; only set-cookie arrives as an array) and both folds are re-split identically downstream — a kolu/drishti design the human must rule"}}
{"id":"bundle-prefix-consumer","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a7","title":"olai follow-up: pass /_olai/assets/ to build + serve once the kolu pin carries #2197, and flip the asserted assets/ 404 test (#341) #kolu-upstream","done":"2026-08-22T11:11:14-04:00","desc":"The consumer half of bundle-reserved-prefix, owed by the lane's own rule (case 3: the socket was upstream). Dispatchable as a small PR once kolu is re-pinned; the human rules when. Not a deferral in the godly sense — a sequenced follow-up.","created":"2026-08-22T03:51:57-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T11:11:14-04:00","custom":{"blocked-on":"an npins bump of kolu to a commit containing 855df636 (surface-app buildSurfaceClient assetPrefix)","from":"#341 + kolu#2197","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/344 — merged 2026-08-22 as dd4b4fe9 (with the kolu pin to 66d38bb2 and upgrade-headers-consumer)","scope":"packages/web/src/build.ts passes assetPrefix '/_olai/assets/' to buildSurfaceClient and the same to serveSurfaceApp; serve.test.ts's to-be-flipped assertion becomes 'a vault file under assets/ opens as a page'; routes.ts's collision paragraph says the collision is gone; docs/format.md? no; website if it mentions the bundle"}}
{"id":"upgrade-headers-consumer","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a8","title":"olai follow-up: read the identity header at the websocket upgrade via serveSurfaceApp's upgradeHeaders once the kolu pin carries #2196 — the chip stops needing GET /olai/who for a tab that is already connected #kolu-upstream","done":"2026-08-22T11:11:15-04:00","desc":"The consumer half of kolu-upgrade-headers. Sequenced follow-up, not a godly deferral; dispatchable together with bundle-prefix-consumer after one kolu pin bump. The human rules when.","created":"2026-08-22T04:43:30-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T11:11:15-04:00","custom":{"blocked-on":"an npins bump of kolu to a commit containing 58c68bdf; the same bump bundle-prefix-consumer waits on — one pin move serves both follow-ups","from":"kolu#2196 (olai #330's ask)","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/344 — merged 2026-08-22 as dd4b4fe9 (identity read off the websocket upgrade as a per-connection who.get procedure; GET /olai/who kept for share sheets)","scope":"olai's serve names OLAI_IDENTITY_* header names in upgradeHeaders, the per-connection services read identity off connection.headers (the ladder from #337 resolves the same way), /olai/who stays for plain-HTTP doors; the kolu PR body's 'one-line consumer change' section says exactly what"}}
{"id":"flaky-tests","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a9","title":"flaky tests — the one sanctioned deferral: a test found flaky on master that a PR does not own","desc":"RULED by the human 2026-08-22 11:57: \"in future, flakes are deferred in Inbox under the 'flaky tests' node\". A PR that meets a timing-shaped test it does not own reports the reproduction in its body under \"Observed\", and the orchestrator files ONE child here per flaky file (what fails, how often, the runs, the PR that saw it) and dispatches it as its own lane. This is the only shape of deferral that is not a stop-and-ask; everything else stays under the No-deferrals rule.","created":"2026-08-22T11:51:06-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T17:03:58-04:00"}
{"id":"runtime-test-flaky","parent":"flaky-tests","ord":"a0","title":"packages/server/src/runtime.test.ts is flaky when its ten tests run together — three races, one possibly a product race","done":"2026-08-22T12:58:13-04:00","desc":"Seen by #343's author on the UNMODIFIED file at 0bc896f7, run alone, three runs = three outcomes: (1) all green; (2) `a reader watching a head is told the file moved` times out at 5 s; (3) `a reader holding a key across a file's birth` FAILS in 25 ms (an assertion, not a timeout) together with `the shelf is answered per revision` timing out. The test opencode first named (`a file whose reader has gone is not re-read on a later revision`) passes standalone 8/8; failures appear only when the file's tests run together. Raising all ten budgets to 15 s was tried and reverted: it converts fast failures into slow ones and fixes none. The 25 ms assertion miss suggests at least one race is in the product (runtime.ts reader/revision bookkeeping), not the test. Goal: make runtime.test.ts deterministic — find each race, decide test-race vs product-race, fix the product where it is the product, and pin it (≥20 consecutive full-file runs green under load). Source: https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/343 body, 'Observed, not deferred'.","created":"2026-08-22T11:51:06-04:00","changed":"2026-08-22T12:58:13-04:00","custom":{"dispatch":"Grok, per the human 11:55 ('dispatch that separately to Grok'); reviewer opencode","from":"#343 (opencode review nit 4 + the author's reproduction), filed 2026-08-22 11:58","pr":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/347 — merged 2026-08-22 as 28703e7b (test races only; watching() attaches before mutating; 20/20 green under load)"}}
{"id":"e2e-localhost-load-flakes","parent":"flaky-tests","ord":"a1","title":"e2e on a loaded localhost: three timing scenarios fail 1–2 per 878 and pass on rerun — html_previews.feature:36, archived_only_in_trash.feature:29, the_sidebar_sticks.feature:36","todo":true,"created":"2026-08-22T17:03:58-04:00","custom":{"from":"#351's CI on localhost 2026-08-22 17:00 (two e2e runs, different scenarios each time; 876/878 then 876/878), while another lane built beside it; also seen today: code_tab mouse-drag on kolu, olai_names_its_own_files:159 capture wait on petit cold","shape":"wall-clock waits (a picture never refused in report.html; agenda-empty timeout; 'page does not scroll in this window') — load artifacts until proven otherwise; each wants the #347 treatment: find what the step waits on and wait on that, not on time"}}
